<title>SLOVENIA: ALPINE SKIING-SYKORA WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-SYKORA WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>KRANJSKA GORA, Slovenia 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian Thomas Sykora won a men's Alpine ski World Cup slalom race on Monday in a time of one minute 41.93 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Frenchman Sebastien Amiez was second in 1:42.29 and Thomas Stangassinger of Austria finished third in 1:42.34.</p>
